# nx-design System Storybook

When the user says "Use nx-design system Storybook", or provides a PRD and asks
to create nx design system UI, use `docs/storybook-agent/agentic-ui-from-prd.md`.

Load these remote sources first:

```text
https://syednoumansyed.github.io/hessa-nx-design-system/agent-manifest/index.json
https://syednoumansyed.github.io/hessa-nx-design-system/agent-manifest/tokens.json
```

Then pick the relevant context pack or component shard from the manifest. Inspect
the selected Storybook `absoluteUrl` iframe links before writing UI code.

Rules:

- Use nx design system components instead of raw HTML controls.
- Use reactive forms. Do not use `ngModel`.
- Use token rules for typography, spacing, colors, radius, RTL, role theming,
  and responsive breakpoints.
- For modal, sheet, sidebar, picker, table, and selector PRDs, validate desktop
  and mobile behavior separately.
- In the final response, list the Storybook stories and token rules used.
- For Storybook, audit, manifest, and agent-instruction work inside this repo,
  target `dev/storybook-agent` rather than `main`.
